  "final_assistant_text": "Implementation complete. Here's a summary of the work:\n\n**Created:** `src/textkit/slugify.py`\n\n```python\n\"\"\"URL slug helper.\"\"\"\n\nimport re\n\n_NON_SLUG_CHARS = re.compile(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\")\n\n\ndef slugify(text: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return a URL-safe slug derived from *text*.\n\n    The text is lowercased, and every run of characters that are not\n    ASCII letters or digits is replaced with a single ``-``. Leading\n    and trailing ``-`` characters are removed. If the text contains no\n    ASCII letters or digits, an empty string is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _NON_SLUG_CHARS.sub(\"-\", text.lower()).strip(\"-\")\n```\n\n**How it meets the requirements:**\n\n1. **Lowercase** via `text.lower()` — uppercase ASCII letters become lowercase and are therefore preserved by the regex.\n2. **Replace runs of non-alphanumerics** via `[^a-z0-9]+` — one or more non-ASCII-letter/digit characters collapse into a single `-`.\n3. **Trim leading/trailing `-`** via `.strip(\"-\")`.\n4. **Empty result for no letters/digits** — for input like `\"!!!  \"`, the whole text becomes a single `-` after substitution, which `strip(\"-\")` reduces to `\"\"`.\n\n**Verification (traced against the examples):**\n- `slugify(\"Hello, World!\")` → `\"hello, world!\"` → `\"hello-world-\"` → `\"hello-world\"` ✓\n- `slugify(\"  Multiple   Spaces  \")` → `\"-multiple-spaces-\"` → `\"multiple-spaces\"` ✓\n\nI also confirmed the file content by re-reading it after writing. One caveat: the task's provided command line (`PYTHONPATH=src python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -t tests`) could not be executed because this environment's policy blocks `run_command` entirely, so I could not run the existing test suite in this session. No existing files were modified, and `README.md`/`tests/` were not touched.",
